          <p>The Midwest has one of the highest concentrations of defined-benefit pension holders in the US — teachers, state employees, city workers, and union members from the automotive, steel, and manufacturing sectors. These pensioners often have strong, stable monthly income that maps well onto the NLV's passive income requirement. Illinois TRS, Wisconsin WRS, Ohio PERS, and Michigan pension recipients are a major applicant group.</p>
