        <h2>Income Requirements &amp; Midwest-Specific Sources</h2>
        <p>The 2026 NLV income threshold is approximately $2,600/month for a single applicant and $4,000/month for a couple — USD approximations of the IPREM-based euro figure. Confirm the current rate at the time of your application.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Common Income Sources for Midwest Applicants</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Social Security:</strong> SSA benefit verification letter plus 3–6 months bank statements confirming deposits.</li>
        <li><strong>Illinois TRS / SERS pension:</strong> Pension award letter and bank statements showing monthly deposits.</li>
        <li><strong>Wisconsin WRS pension:</strong> Award letter and bank statement confirmation of regular deposits.</li>
        <li><strong>Ohio PERS / STRS pension:</strong> Pension documentation plus bank statements.</li>
        <li><strong>Michigan pension (public employees):</strong> MPSERS or similar — award letter plus statements.</li>
        <li><strong>UAW / Teamsters / other union pensions:</strong> Union pension documentation plus bank statements.</li>
        <li><strong>401(k) / IRA distributions:</strong> Regular, scheduled distributions — not lump sums. Account and bank statements required.</li>
        <li><strong>Investment income:</strong> Dividends, interest, and capital gains from brokerage accounts.</li>
        <li><strong>Midwest rental income:</strong> Schedule E from Form 1040 plus lease agreements and bank deposit confirmation.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--warn">
