          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Purchase Spanish Private Health Insurance</h3>
            <p>Buy a policy from a Spain-registered insurer: established private health insurers in Spain, or a leading private insurer. The policy must cover you without copays and with no exclusions for pre-existing conditions. Medicare does not satisfy this requirement. The policy must be in place before your appointment.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">05</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Assemble Your Financial Documentation</h3>
            <p>Gather 6 months of bank statements, pension award letters, SSA benefit verification, most recent Form 1040, brokerage and investment statements, and any other proof of passive income. Obtain certified Spanish translations for all key documents. Organize everything into a clean, clearly labeled file.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">06</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Complete Form EX-01 (Visa Application Form)</h3>
            <p>Download Spain's national long-stay visa application form (EX-01). Fill in all fields completely in Spanish, or provide a certified translation. Print and sign two originals. Date the form close to your appointment — not weeks in advance.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">07</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Attend In-Person Appointment in Chicago</h3>
            <p>Appear in person at the Consulate General of Spain, 180 N Michigan Ave, Suite 1500, Chicago, IL 60601. Bring all original documents plus copies. Pay the consulate visa fee (approximately €80–€100, typically by money order). Biometrics may be collected at this appointment.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__step">
          <div class="msv__step-num">08</div>
          <div class="msv__step-body">
            <h3>Await Decision &amp; Collect Visa</h3>
            <p>Processing takes 10–16 weeks. You'll be notified when a decision is made. Collect your visa in person or via an authorized representative. Travel to Spain within the visa's validity window and register at your local Foreigners' Office (Oficina de Extranjeros) within 30 days of arrival.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

